    {
      "id": "e02",
      "time_offset_ms": 46850,
      "type": "show_schema",
      "target": "sql_viewer",
      "params": {},
      "narration": "You asked A-I to get your Q four revenue. It wrote a query, you ran it, got a big number, sent it to your boss, felt like a genius. One problem, that number was the entire year. The A-I forgot a single line, a WHERE clause, and you didn't know enough S-Q-L to catch it. If you're a marketer, a founder, a student, anyone who's thinking A-I means you'll never need to learn S-Q-L, this is the one minute that'll change your mind. Here's a sales table with columns like rep name, client, quarter, and amount, basically a receipt book for every deal your team closed all year.",
      "transition": "new_concept",
      "clears": [],
      "phases": []
    },
    {
